From 3a1279f951681bf31574757aedacfc610cfa7385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:24:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 58/70] CUDA/HIP: kvq attention applies the output FWHT (+ q8_1
 for the o projection) in its combine launch (GGML_HIP_KVQ_FWHT)

With a rotated KV cache the attention output goes through a Hadamard MUL_MAT (FWHT kernel) and,
for the o projection, quantize_q8_1. When the kvq kernel runs with a KV split, its combine launch
(flash_attn_kvq_combine_fwht) now also does both: the row as flash_attn_combine_results (body
refactored into flash_attn_combine_results_value, shared), its FWHT by the first warp with
fwht_row_warp as fwht_cuda, the q8_1 copy with quantize_q8_1_group into the producer target of the
q8_1 cache. Both the attention output and the FWHT output are still written. 336 -> 316 kernels
per LFM2 token; combine+FWHT+q8_1 3.1 us vs 1.7 + 1.1 + 1.8 us.

Bitwise: logit hashes of 64 greedy steps unchanged (KV q8_0 kvq depth 0 / 3000 a7ce25b73f887fed /
b47452b9380b665b, vec a3c06fe69758819e (not fused), KV q4_0 b81cc99db07e6661 (fused too)).
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, LFM2.5-24B-A2B, KV q8_0, 3 rounds interleaved: 3.928 -> 3.879 ms/token.
GGML_HIP_KVQ_FWHT=0: separate launches. test-backend-ops: ATTN_PREP now ends with the output
rotation and the o projection 3/3 (also with the switch off), FLASH_ATTN_EXT 4060/4060.
